zune-jpeg: make the blocks after a marker that cuts an MCU row short neutral

`inner_decode_mcu_width` (mcu.rs) stops the MCU row when a marker ends the
entropy data, and the blocks after that column keep whatever the row buffer
held: the previous MCU row's samples in a one-shot decode, but the blocks an
earlier suspended incremental attempt decoded from the zero padding past the
end of the visible data when the decode resumed (MCU-row checkpoints reuse
the buffers on purpose). The same bytes then render differently in one-shot
and incremental mode ("incremental pixels diverge from one-shot decode").
Fill the undecoded rest of the row with the neutral sample 128 (what an
all-zero block decodes to) for the scan's components, so both modes render
the cut row the same way. Only streams with a marker inside an MCU row are
affected. Includes a regression test (tests/incremental_resume.rs).

Not fixed upstream as of zune-image 2cdbbf5.
Upstream: open #506 (recover sequential component scans; "roll back
speculative row writes on suspension") addresses the suspended-row writes
more generally.

diff --git a/crates/zune-jpeg/src/mcu.rs b/crates/zune-jpeg/src/mcu.rs
index 1aef873c..3042edd9 100644
--- a/crates/zune-jpeg/src/mcu.rs
+++ b/crates/zune-jpeg/src/mcu.rs
@@ -1110,6 +1110,7 @@ impl<T: ZByteReaderTrait> JpegDecoder<T> {
             scan_du_width = scan_du_width.min(min_du);
         }
 
+        let mut decoded_until = scan_du_width;
         for j in start_col..scan_du_width {
             // iterate over components
             for &k in z_scans {
@@ -1286,6 +1287,7 @@ impl<T: ZByteReaderTrait> JpegDecoder<T> {
                             "DNL marker found before the end of an MCU row",
                         ));
                     }
+                    decoded_until = j + 1;
                     break;
                 }
                 continue;
@@ -1297,6 +1299,7 @@ impl<T: ZByteReaderTrait> JpegDecoder<T> {
                         "DNL marker found before the end of an MCU row",
                     ));
                 }
+                decoded_until = j + 1;
                 break;
             }
 
@@ -1306,10 +1309,33 @@ impl<T: ZByteReaderTrait> JpegDecoder<T> {
                         "DNL marker found before the end of an MCU row",
                     ));
                 }
+                decoded_until = j + 1;
                 break;
             }
         }
 
+        // A marker that ends the entropy data before the end of the MCU row
+        // leaves the remaining blocks of the row undecoded. Make them neutral
+        // instead of leaving whatever an earlier row or a suspended
+        // incremental attempt wrote there, so a resumed decode renders the
+        // same row as a one-shot decode.
+        if !PROGRESSIVE && decoded_until < scan_du_width {
+            for &k in z_scans {
+                let component = &mut self.components[k];
+                if !component.needed || component.width_stride == 0 {
+                    continue;
+                }
+                let rows = if SAMPLED { component.vertical_sample * 8 } else { 8 };
+                let first_col = decoded_until * component.horizontal_sample * 8;
+                let width_stride = component.width_stride;
+                for row in component.raw_coeff.chunks_exact_mut(width_stride).take(rows) {
+                    if let Some(rest) = row.get_mut(first_col..) {
+                        rest.fill(128);
+                    }
+                }
+            }
+        }
+
         self.check_stream_marker_after_mcu_width(stream, is_last_row, mcu_row)
     }
 
